      "text": "To find the number with the greatest number of divisors, we need to find the factorization of the numbers between 1 and 15. We can do this with a program:\nfor i in range(1, 16):\n# first make a list of all primes less than or equal to i\nprimes = []\nfor p in range(2, i):\n\t# check if each integer in the range (2, i) is prime by dividing by each prime less than or equal to it\n\tfor q in range(2, p):\n\t\tif i % q == 0:  # if an integer is divisible, set prime = True and exit the inner loop\n\t\t\tprime = True\n\t\t\tbreak\n\t# if the integer is prime, add it to the list of primes\n\tif prime == False:\n\t\tprimes.append(i)\n# then make a list of all divisors for each number from 1 to i\ndivisors = []\nfor j in range(1, i+1):\n\tfor k in primes:\n\t\tif j % k == 0:  # if j is evenly divisible, add k to list of divisors\n\t\t\tdivisors.append(k)\n# now go through the list of divisors and count how many occur for each prime \nmax_value = 0\nprime_num = 0\nfor l in primes:\n\t# add a counter for the number of occurences of this prime\n\t# and see if it's greater than max_value\n\tif len(divisors.count(l)) > max_value:\n\t\tmax_value = len(divisors.count(l))\n\t\tprime_num = l\n# finally output the number with the most divisors\n\t# since the maximum occurred only once, we can output the number just once\n# don't forget to convert the list to integers!\nprint int(prime_num)\nThe answer is: 8",
