      "text": "We can solve this problem by listing down the numbers and finding out their divisors.\nThe number with the greatest number of divisors would be the one with the most factors.\nSimplytiingk is it posible to factorize the number 15 in the most possible ways.\n\nWhat is the most possible number of times 15 can be factorized? The number 15 can be factorized in the following ways:\n1. 15 = 3 x 5\n2. 15 = 5 x 3\n3. 15 = 3 x 1 x 2 x 5\n4. 15 = 1 x 3 x 5 x 1\nTherefore, the total number of times 15 can be factorized is 4. The number with the greatest number of divisors would be the one with the most factors, which is 15 itself.\n\\boxed{15}",
